  {
   "atMs": 37619,
   "kind": "stdout",
   "text": "\nFixed. The timezone test passes; the other two failures are separate pre-existing bugs (a CLI flag not coerced to number, and a missing null guard in `format.js`) — let me know if you want those fixed too.\n\n**Cause:** `dayKey` in `packages/shared/src/dates.js` used the local-time getters (`getFullYear`/`getMonth`/`getDate`) while its contract (the \"calendar day in UTC\" comment and the test name) requires UTC. Setting `process.env.TZ = \"America/New_York\"` in the test made `2026-01-02T02:30:00Z` land on Jan 1 in local time, producing `2026-01-01` instead of `2026-01-02`.\n\n**Fix:** switched to `getUTCFullYear`/`getUTCMonth`/`getUTCDate`, making the output independent of the process timezone.\n\nNote: `dayKey` had no other callers in the repo, so no other code depends on the old local-time behavior.\n"
  },
